cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  RTpipeline 3.0.0 is a published release. Cite it by version and by the DOI
  archived for the v3.0.0 tag. When the bytes you ran differ from the tag, also
  report the immutable git commit or container digest. Cite TotalSegmentator,
  PyRadiomics and, for imported structures, RTsegmentator and each segmentation
  model as well.
title: "RTpipeline: Automated Radiotherapy DICOM Processing Pipeline"
type: software
version: 3.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-25
license: MIT
authors:
- family-names: Stawiski
  given-names: Konrad
repository-code: https://github.com/kstawiski/rtpipeline
url: https://kstawiski.github.io/rtpipeline/
abstract: >-
  RTpipeline turns raw radiotherapy DICOM exports into analysis-ready cohort
  tables. It organizes CT, RTSTRUCT, RTPLAN, RTDOSE and RT treatment records into
  validated patient courses, adds standardized structures from TotalSegmentator,
  local nnU-Net models and the RTsegmentator portal, and computes dose-volume
  histogram metrics, PyRadiomics features with NTCV perturbation robustness,
  multimodal biomarkers and quality-control reports, with completion receipts
  that bind each output to its inputs and configuration.
keywords:
- radiotherapy
- DICOM RT
- dose-volume histogram
- radiomics
- auto-segmentation
- reproducibility
- Snakemake
